.         /* We assume that PoliticalAttitude, a continuous measure reverse-cod
> ed such that higher values indicate stronger left-wing political attitudes, r
> eflects support for gender equality (Hypothesis 2). 
>    Accordingly, we run a random-effects linear panel regression with Politica
> lAttitude as the dependent variable and DaughterHH (categorical: child gender
>  composition) as the key independent variable. 
>    Control variables include gender (Woman), number of children, partnership 
> status, sexual orientation, parental religion (mother/father), age, and regio
> n. 
>    We use panel-robust standard errors and cluster at the individual level (p
> id).
>         */
. 
. 
. 
. * EXTRACT AND EXPORT RESULTS * (Please check whether the suggested code autom
> atically picks up the correct statistics for your chosen regression analysis 
> and adapt if needed)
. 
.                 * Extract the required statistics
. 
.                 * (i) coefficient estimate
.                 local coefficient = _b[3.DaughterHH]

. 
.                 * (ii) standard error
.                 local se = _se[3.DaughterHH]

. 
.                 * (iii) family of the test statistic (e.g. z, t, F, Chi²)
.                 local test_stat_family = "z" // Adapted by DA during consiste
> ncy check

. 
.                 * (iv) residual and model degrees of freedom (DFs) if applica
> ble
.                 local df_residual = e(df_r)

.                 local df_model = e(df_m)

. 
.                 * (v) p-value
.                 // local p_value = _b[3.DaughterHH] / _se[3.DaughterHH]
.                 // local p_value = 2 * ttail(e(df_r), abs(`p_value'))
.                 // Calculate z-statistic
.                 local zstat = abs(_b[3.DaughterHH] / _se[3.DaughterHH])

.                 // Two-sided p-value
.                 local p_value = 2 * (1 - normal(`zstat'))

.                 
.                 * (vi) number of observations
.                 local num_obs = e(N)

. 
.                 * (vii) number of participants
.                 quietly levelsof pid if e(sample), local(participants)

.                 local num_participants : word count `participants'

. 
.                 * (viii) interpretation of directionality
.                 scalar coef_d_daughter = _b[3.DaughterHH]

.                 local interpretation "positive coefficient is in line with hy
> pothesis"

. 
.         // Display the saved statistics
.         di "Coefficient: `coefficient'"
Coefficient: -.0219197717421621

.         di "Standard Error: `se'"
Standard Error: .0375436836642019

.         di "Test Statistic Family: `test_stat_family'"
Test Statistic Family: z

.         di "Residual Degrees of Freedom: `df_residual'"
Residual Degrees of Freedom: .

.         di "Model Degrees of Freedom: `df_model'"
Model Degrees of Freedom: 15

.         di "p-value: " `p_value'
p-value: .55932317

.         di "Number of observations: " `num_obs'
Number of observations: 49801

.         di      "Number of participants: " `num_participants'
Number of participants: 18064

.         di "Interpretation of directionality: " "`interpretation'"
Interpretation of directionality: positive coefficient is in line with hypothes
> is

. 
.         * Export results to csv 
.         file open myfile using "$OUT/h2_results.csv", write replace
(file C:\Users\dalbrecht\Research
    Projects\ManyDaughters\ManyDaughters_DataPreprocessing/data/derived/95_re
    > sults/h2_results.csv not found)

.         file write myfile "coefficient,se,family,residual_df,model_df,p_value
> ,num_obs,num_participants,interpretation" _n

.         file write myfile "`coefficient', `se', `test_stat_family', `df_resid
> ual', `df_model',`p_value',`num_obs',`num_participants',`interpretation'" _n

.         file close myfile

. 
